# Phase 17 jstack concurrency correction — 2026-10-13T17:08:36Z

- Branch: `phase/18-phase-17-admin-query`. The Java reference checkout remains read-only; plans remain unchanged.
- Reproduced a `jstackEnable` gap on Linux ARM64: concurrent Running Info captures could hit `try_lock`, making one request fall back to a current-thread-only dump. Added a barrier-controlled regression first; it failed with `another Linux stack capture is in progress`.
- Serialized process-wide stack captures on macOS, Linux, and Windows. The Linux regression starts two simultaneous readers and verifies that both dumps retain a named worker and readable frames. Linux signal-handler tests now hold the capture lock while installing/checking handlers, avoiding test races with other Running Info captures. Windows and Apple capture paths use the same mutex ownership rule.
- The first post-fix run found Linux `comm` truncates thread names to 15 bytes; shortened the test marker. A later full Linux run exposed that the existing default-signal restoration assertion sampled the process-wide handler outside the capture lock; moved the snapshot, capture, and assertion under one lock and retained the custom-handler restoration case.
- PASS on macOS AArch64: `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-consumer --locked` (164 unit tests plus all consumer integration/doc targets); strict consumer Clippy with all targets/features; `cargo fmt --all -- --check`.
- PASS on Linux ARM64 with Rust 1.85.0: both `stack::tests` pass; the Phase 18 continuation's `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked` passes after the correction; strict `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings` passes. The full Linux runs used Debian Bookworm in Docker, not GitHub Ubuntu CI.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_17_ADMIN_MATRIX.md` with the capture serialization behavior and new evidence. Native Windows runtime behavior remains an environment check. The broader Phase 6 source/API/input audit and current Ubuntu CI result remain open in Phase 18; Phase 19 Broker/Docker scenarios remain separately pending.
